# webOS TV knowledge (mandatory for client work)

Hooks enforce this when editing under `apps/loon/client/`. Do not skip it.

## Before webOS client implementation

After project + context memory (see `nest-memory.mdc`), call:

**`search_knowledge_base`** (`nest-knowledge`) with `collection="webos-tv"`

Search for the specific APIs or platform behavior you need **before** guessing. Examples:

| Task | Example query |
|------|----------------|
| Packaging | `appinfo.json mandatory id icon version` |
| Back / D-pad | `disableBackHistoryAPI back button` |
| Lifecycle | `webOSRelaunch handlesRelaunch` |
| Install on TV | `ares-install developer mode passphrase` |
| App type | `packaged web app basic hosted` |

Run **at least one** `webos-tv` search per session before editing client code. Re-search when touching a new platform area (player, packaging, events).

## During work

- Prefer indexed LG docs over training-data assumptions.
- Cite behavior from search results; link [webOS Developer](https://webostv.developer.lge.com) for humans.
- If search returns nothing useful, say so and fetch may need `./scripts/fetch-webos-knowledge.sh --force`.

## Refresh index

```bash
./scripts/fetch-webos-knowledge.sh          # from nest repo root
```

See [apps/loon/docs/webos-knowledge-v1.md](../../apps/loon/docs/webos-knowledge-v1.md).
